# colcon output. Regenerated by `colcon build`; never source-controlled.
ros2_ws/build/
ros2_ws/install/
ros2_ws/log/


# Derived intermediates -- the OBJ+MTL+texture a GLB capture is converted into by
# mesh_import.py. Regenerated from the capture on demand and keyed by its hash, so
# committing them would only duplicate the raw scan at full size.
simulation/photogrammetry/work/

# Training artefacts (Task 4 onwards)
rl/runs/
rl/checkpoints/
*.zip

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Vendored ROS 2 sources. Each carries its own .git, so committing them here would record
# bare gitlinks with no submodule config -- a clone that arrives with five empty
# directories and no error. They are pinned by exact commit in ros2_ws/src/vendor.repos
# instead, and the one that is modified (pepper_ign_moveit2, ported to Humble/Fortress
# with the sensors added) also ships as a patch in ros2_ws/src/patches/.
# Everything in ros2_ws/src that this project *authors* is committed -- see the
# un-ignore rules below.
ros2_ws/src/*
!ros2_ws/src/vendor.repos
!ros2_ws/src/patches/
!ros2_ws/src/pepper_room_description/

# Stray files from a mis-quoted docker command inside the vendored fork. Harmless, but
# 'git add' on a file literally named '[' is a trap worth disarming permanently.
ros2_ws/src/pepper_ign_moveit2/

# The RL virtualenv. Created with --system-site-packages so rclpy/cv_bridge still import;
# numpy is pinned at 1.26.4 rather than 2.x.
.venv/

# Benchmark and evaluation output. Reproducible by re-running, and the numbers that
# matter get written up rather than committed.
rl/reports/

rl/cache/body_randomisation/

# The pose tracker's calibration (rl/env/pose_tracker.py) is tied to exactly where one
# physical camera is mounted and exactly how one tag is stuck to the robot -- committing
# it would silently offer it as if it applied to a different camera position, which it
# does not. It is also entirely machine-generated (rl/scripts/calibrate_pose_tracker.py
# writes it; nobody should hand-edit it), so unlike the ground_truth/TEMPLATE files there
# is no hand-authored template worth shipping -- the schema is documented in
# rl/env/pose_tracker.py's save_calibration/load_calibration instead.
rl/config/pose_tracker_calibration.json

# Safety copies written by the mesh tools before they rewrite a file in place
# (tools/mesh_level.py -> *.prelevel, tools/mesh_flatten_floor.py -> *.preflatten) and
# hand backups. The manifest records every transform applied, so these are for undoing a
# step locally, not for the record.
*.prelevel
*.preflatten
*.bak



report/editor/build/

# LaTeX build output (main.pdf and main.bbl are kept so the report reads without a build)
report/latex/*.aux
report/latex/*.blg
report/latex/*.fdb_latexmk
report/latex/*.fls
report/latex/*.log
report/latex/*.out
report/latex/*.synctex.gz

# Local assistant config and environment files. Note: match dotenv files only -- a bare
# "env" pattern would also swallow the rl/env/ source package.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.mcp.json
.env
.env.*
